{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795000844,"nonce":"Q2+ANv1nmDrs4IkOfJ0PpyBp7hg=","message":"Implemented core logging without a standalone crate/haxelib: hxn::log exports Rust level macros/functions; hxn.Log, LogLevel and LogRecord are core Haxe classes included in CLI support and the haxelib. Both use Off/Error/Warn/Info/Debug/Trace, runtime filtering, source target/file/line, Unix-millisecond timestamps, origin and UTF-8 truncation metadata. The app owns one Haxe sink; null uses diagnostic output (Android hxcpp logcat, other native/wasm host stderr, JS console).\n\nThe dependency-free hxn-abi contains a safe bounded queue/wire transport, re-exported by hxn. It gains no exported C symbol. Generated adapters export library-prefixed log_level/log_take and register capture through the library support class, retained under full DCE and namespace-only consumers. Native workers retain no host callback. Queues hold 256 records, message/target/file bounds are 8192/256/1024 UTF-8 bytes, overflow reports drops, and empty drains avoid payload allocations. Rust macros skip disabled arguments/targets. Frame loops using Loop.manual batch frontend/native diagnostics at Loop.sync rather than polling native logs after each call; explicit flush and exit still drain. Sink recursion/errors are contained, and conversion/callback/typed-error state is complete before handlers run.\n\nVerification: Rust workspace tests, fmt and clippy passed on Mac and Linux NUC; concurrent logger tests repeated on Linux. ABI Miri passed with seeds 1 and 2 (37 tests each), future Miri passed (38), using ignore-leaks for the pool and disabled isolation for wall-clock access. Counter hand-written/generated bindings passed native and wasm modes: Ash hybrid/JIT/interpreter, hxcpp, CPPIA, Ash wasm threaded/unthreaded and Emscripten threaded/unthreaded; stock HashLink passed on Linux. Core Haxe logging passes standalone eval and JavaScript. Filtering, lazy arguments/string conversion, Unicode bounds, drops, namespace-only/full DCE, reentrant/failing sinks, typed-error preservation, worker delivery and common clocks are exercised. Final generated-runtime runs also cover manual-loop batching.\n\nCLI new/check/run/package and installed consumer tests passed; examples passed native/wasm, both threaded modes and page modes; C import passed native/CPPIA/Emscripten; web timers/futures passed Node and browser with/without threads. Real logging capture/default output/timestamps pass on iOS 17.5 simulator and Android emulator for both Ash and hxcpp, with unique console probes to exclude stale logcat output. The mobile helper stays under tests/counter. Two native libraries share one sink without duplicate records under full DCE on HashLink and hxcpp. Focused native/frontend/worker capture and clocks pass Chrome pages in all four wasm configurations.\n\nAn extra full-counter threaded Ash Chrome run fails at the old bool/float future check; unchanged HEAD reproduces it, so it predates logging. Evidence is recorded separately in 9ee1bd477447c930576c8b0740749b3be5408ab73ab6795c8d011426e90f7435. Do not report that full-counter browser run as passing. Safari WebDriver is unavailable because Allow remote automation is disabled; settings were not changed. Windows CI and physical mobile devices were not run for this change. Keep this issue open for remaining CI/platform validation.\n\nCurrent design/conventions, core layout and hxn skill updated. Rust API docs and an unreleased Haxe API preview regenerated locally (target/log-reference, 20 pages/18 types). CLI-only attribution inventory refreshed with unchanged dependency scope; no logging dependency was added. Work remains uncommitted/unreleased; no source or git-bug push performed.","files":null}]}